@@ -345,3 +345,11 @@
 4. SIGKILL if still running
 
 Tasks from gracefully shutdown workers reset to `todo` for retry on the next wave. Crashed workers (non-graceful exit) block the task in autonomous mode to prevent retry loops.
+
+## Live peer communication constraints
+
+- A task dependency gates process startup, not just file access. Never require task A to message task B before A completes when B depends on A: B cannot be online.
+- For bidirectional messaging, start both peers in the same wave without task dependencies; wait for a file/message with a bounded timeout (60 seconds), and keep the sender alive until the reply arrives. For sequential tasks use durable task artifacts, not direct replies to an exited worker.
+- Resolve actual registered peer names using list; a model name such as GLM is not automatically a peer name.
+- Assign explicit provider/model per task when different workers must use different models. Role-level worker defaults apply to ALL worker tasks, including tasks titled GLM.
+- Offline send is failure, not queued delivery. Report it and block when the required peer cannot start; do not repeatedly poll or claim success.
